        "title": "Redesign settings as a System Settings-style split view",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nComplete redesign of the settings window in the System Settings idiom:\n\n- **One sidebar for everything** — a `NavigationSplitView` sidebar lists the app panes (General, Display, Advanced, About, Debug) with colored icon chips *and* every provider as a first-class row: brand icon, live status dot, refresh spinner, dimmed when disabled, searchable, drag-to-reorder, enable/disable via context menu. The old Providers tab with its nested inner sidebar is gone.\n- **Native grouped forms everywhere** — General/Display/Advanced/About *and the provider detail pane* are rebuilt on `Form` + `.formStyle(.grouped)` with trailing switches, `LabeledContent` info rows, native picker rows, and section footers, replacing the hand-rolled `SettingsCard`/`PreferenceControlRow`/`PreferenceSwitchRow`/`ProviderSettingsSection` stack and the label-width measurement machinery. Captions survive only where they genuinely explain something.\n- **Content regrouped by intent** — General = language/terminal/login + refresh + notifications + menu shortcut + quit; Display = menu bar icon, menu content, cost summary, animations; Advanced = only genuinely advanced things (CLI install, privacy, keychain, diagnostics). Cost-fetch status lines moved out of the rows into a section footer.\n- **One resizable window** — 920×640 by default, user-resizable down to 780×520; the per-tab resize/animation machinery (`PreferencesTabLayoutCoordinator`, window-frame walking) is deleted.\n- **Selection is remembered** — the last selected pane (including a specific provider) persists across launches; the menu's \"Settings…\" restores it instead of forcing General.\n\nNet: the diff removes more code than it adds, and all 21 locales gained translations for the nine new strings (strict locales ar/fa/th included).\n\n## Before → After\n\n| | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| General | ![before general](https://artifacts.openclaw.ai/pr/codexbar-1853/before-general.png) | ![after general](https://artifacts.openclaw.ai/pr/codexbar-1853/after-general.png) |\n| Providers | ![before providers](https://artifacts.openclaw.ai/pr/codexbar-1853/before-providers.png) | ![after claude](https://artifacts.openclaw.ai/pr/codexbar-1853/after-claude.png) |\n| Display | ![before display](https://artifacts.openclaw.ai/pr/codexbar-1853/before-display.png) | ![after display](https://artifacts.openclaw.ai/pr/codexbar-1853/after-display.png) |\n| Advanced | ![before advanced](https://artifacts.openclaw.ai/pr/codexbar-1853/before-advanced.png) | ![after advanced](https://artifacts.openclaw.ai/pr/codexbar-1853/after-advanced.png) |\n\nNotes:\n- The provider detail pane was further aligned to grouped forms after the Providers after-shot above was uploaded (info rows as `LabeledContent`, full-width usage bars, native picker rows, no more State row). A refreshed screenshot is pending an artifact-store auth refresh.\n- [About before](https://artifacts.openclaw.ai/pr/codexbar-1853/before-about.png) gets the same treatment: centered hero above grouped Updates and Links sections with a copyright footer (after-shot upload also pending the auth refresh).\n- Screenshots are hosted on the artifact store, not committed to the repo; the two PNGs the previous revision added under `docs/screenshots/` are removed. Usage figures in the Providers before-shot are redacted.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `make check` — SwiftFormat/SwiftLint/locale checks clean\n- `swift test --filter \"PreferencesPaneSmokeTests|ProvidersPaneCoverageTests|PreferencesSelectionTests|CodexAccountsSettingsSectionTests|SettingsWindowAppearanceTests\"` — pass\n- `make test` — full sharded suite green (earlier runs surfaced two test-inventory fixes now included: the Italian \"Privacy\" allowlist and retargeted sidebar localization markers; two aborted runs were CPU-contention shard timeouts, rerun clean)\n- `./Scripts/compile_and_run.sh` / `package_app.sh` — live QA of General, Display, Advanced, About, and Claude provider panes against the packaged app; pane persistence and menu-restore verified live\n- pre-push autoreview (Codex, gpt-5.5): two runs (main redesign commit + provider-pane alignment), both clean\n",
        "branch": "codex/restructure-settings",
